  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "How many ways can the letters of the word TOPOLOGICAL be arranged if",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the O’s are all together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$181\\,440$",
          "worked": "Treat OOO as one element. There are nine elements, including two identical L’s.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{9!}{2!}\\\\N&=181\\,440.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the O’s are together, and the L’s are together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$40\\,320$",
          "worked": "Treat OOO and LL as single elements. The eight resulting elements are distinct.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=8!\\\\N&=40\\,320.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q16-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the O’s are all separate.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1\\,693\\,440$\n\nArrange the other letters, then place the O’s in three different gaps.",
          "worked": "Arrange the eight non-O letters, allowing for the two identical L’s. These letters create nine gaps, including the ends. Put one O in each of three different gaps; divide by $3!$ because the O’s are identical.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{8!}{2!}\\times\\frac{9\\times8\\times7}{3!}\\\\N&=1\\,693\\,440.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q16-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "two of the O’s are together, but the third O is separate.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1\\,451\\,520$\n\nPlace the OO block and the single O in different gaps.",
          "worked": "Arrange the eight non-O letters, allowing for the two identical L’s. There are nine gaps for the OO block and then eight different gaps for the single O. The block and single O are distinct elements, so no further factorial division is needed.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{8!}{2!}\\times9\\times8\\\\N&=1\\,451\\,520.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
